IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qld-part12b-fee-units`

-- Tests for Part 12B (qld-part12b-fee-units.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 12B`

#ASSERT `a regulation may prescribe the amount to be the value of a fee unit (s 48B(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a regulation may prescribe the amount to be the value of a fee unit (s 48B(1))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) and its example: the amount of $1.015 may be prescribed.
-- src:980 | Example—
-- src:981 | The amount of $1.015 may be prescribed.
@ref s 48B(2), example (src:980-981)
#ASSERT `the amount prescribed may include a fraction of a cent (s 48B(2))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a regulation may prescribe different amounts for different Acts (s 48B(3))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a regulation may prescribe different amounts for different Acts (s 48B(3))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS The value of a fee unit for an Act is the amount prescribed, or $1 if no amount is prescribed (s 48B(4)).
#ASSERT `the value of a fee unit for an Act (s 48B(4))` (JUST 1.015) EQUALS 1.015
#ASSERT `the value of a fee unit for an Act (s 48B(4))` NOTHING EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the value of a fee unit for an Act (s 48B(4))` (JUST 2) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `an Act may express a fee or other matter as a number of fee units (s 48C(1))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act may also provide for how an amount is to be rounded (s 48C(2))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 48C(3), example: a fee unit of $1.015 and a licence fee of 120.44 fee units: 1.015 x 120.44 = 122.2466, rounded to the nearest cent, $122.25.
-- src:994 | Example—
-- src:995 | A regulation under section 48B prescribes $1.015 to be the value of a fee unit for an Act. The Act provides for a licence fee of 120.44 fee units and does not provide for how amounts are to be rounded for the purpose of this subsection. The number of dollars obtained by multiplying $1.015 by 120.44 is $122.2466. So, after rounding, the amount of the licence fee is $122.25.
@ref s 48C(3), example (src:994-995)
#ASSERT `the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` 1.015 120.44 NOTHING EQUALS 122.25
-- one-half rounds upwards: 0.005 dollars is 0.01; 0.004 is 0.00
#ASSERT `the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` 0.005 1 NOTHING EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` 0.004 1 NOTHING EQUALS 0
-- when the Act provides for how the result is to be rounded, in that way (here to the next whole dollar, 123)
#ASSERT `the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` 1.015 120.44 (JUST 123) EQUALS 123
-- the default value of $1 per fee unit
#ASSERT `the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` 1 50.5 NOTHING EQUALS 50.5
